{
  "_about": "Weltzcraft merch: every product comes in every logo. A buyer picks product, color, logo and size. scripts/merch-build.mjs + scripts/merch_place.py turn this into placed print files, real Printful mockups (weltzcraft-site/img/merch/<product>-<color>-<logo>.webp) and Printful store products (weltzcraft-site/merch-catalog.json). 'tone' picks the logo file: light logos on dark goods, dark logos on light goods. 'box' = [width, height] the logo is fitted into, as shares of the print area (times the logo's own 'scale'); 'top' = gap from the top as a share of its height (no 'top' = centered); 'wrap' prints the logo twice (both sides of a mug). 'price' is US dollars; 2XL adds $2, 3XL adds $3. A logo's 'hat' files replace its normal ones on embroidered items (bigger, bolder lettering that stitches cleanly). A product's 'logos' limits it to those logos; logos marked 'solo' are only used where a product lists them. A 'tint' logo is one-color art recolored to the color's 'ink' (or a default per tone); 'cx' moves the logo sideways (share of the print area, default centered); a logo's 'threads' limits its embroidery thread colors. 'extra' adds more print spots to a product (e.g. a sleeve): each has its own file, box, top and tint.",
